  "description": "Matched 60^3 context and RL-activation comparison using the encoder-corrected best 8D seed C. All five learned branches share the exact matrix/RHS stream, seed offset 2000029, candidate schedule and controller seeds. Default plus five joint branches; no setup-only bandit branch. 3D means three log diffusion coefficients plus a separate intercept (4 stored context entries); 4D additionally includes their mean (5 stored entries). The historical 8D branch retains its original implementation and fixed 1000-problem prefix. Compact contexts are applied to both learners. Dynamic branches use the predeclared reliability-mixture gate with p_bad=0.05, p_good=0.01, delta=0.05 per branch and weights 1/[t(t+1)]; first-attempt failures count before recovery, and RL begins on the next problem after crossing. There is no forced activation deadline. These gate rates are design choices, not retrospectively fitted thresholds. All 5000 problems, recurring learner overhead and recovery count in the comparison.",
